        "title": "refactor(ui): remove dead exports",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe shrink-only dead-export ratchet carried 360 `ui/` entries on current `main`, allowing unused Control UI exports to remain indefinitely. The task began at 365; five original entries landed independently while this branch repeatedly absorbed current-main drift.\n\nCloses #105791\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Internalize unused Control UI symbols and delete helpers or tests that existed only for those exports.\n- Keep meaningful behavior coverage through production-owned modules and public component boundaries.\n- Split custom-element registration side effects where production consumers need implementation exports.\n- Preserve current-main Gateway, lazy-shell, navigation, and device-inventory refactors.\n- Regenerate the baseline with no remaining entry whose path starts with `ui/`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo intended user-visible behavior change. The Control UI exposes a smaller internal module surface while retaining reconnect, registration, chat, workspace, plugin, navigation, and lazy-shell behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Final exact-main baseline reconciliation: 3,307 entries to 2,947; exactly 360 `ui/` entries removed; zero non-UI removals and zero additions.\n- Combined task result: all 365 originally observed UI entries are gone; five landed independently on `main`, and this PR removes the remaining 360.\n- The implementation audit covered all original findings: declarations were internalized/deleted, or implementation exports gained production callers through registration and lazy-loader boundaries.\n- `pnpm test:ui`: 238 files, 3,538 tests passed.\n- `pnpm tsgo:ui`, `pnpm tsgo:test:ui`, and `pnpm build` passed.\n- Focused Control UI Chromium E2E: 7 files, 77 tests passed, covering chat flow, session management, sidebar customization, approval routing, login gating, initial connection, and mount recovery.\n- Remote proof: [Crabbox run run_2c616159ce2d](https://crabbox.openclaw.ai/portal/runs/run_2c616159ce2d).\n- The ratchet was rebuilt from exact `main` at `1577c285009f14bb3fa2ead4c96aab6a8aacd297`; the resulting module loads with 2,947 entries and zero `ui/` paths. `git diff --check` passed.\n- Final published tree: `6497c9395d482d1773da9d83d0ae19d51daae4b6`.\n- Exact PR head: `cce979ecf7f6039c12bdd9e3b159734e9948bca0`; hosted CI and exact-head Mantis browser proof are pending.\n- The whole branch exceeds the autoreview helper's fail-closed bundle limit; coherent production, registration, page/baseline, and test/lib surface reviews were clean. Fresh exact-head retries were blocked by the review service's outbound transport.\n- Actual built-Gateway lifecycle smoke could not be rerun after the final rebase because the task sandbox blocked outbound Crabbox/AWS access. Chromium E2E and Mantis use the repository's mocked Gateway harness; hosted CI is the final exact-head gate.\n",
